("v23", "type", "String")
("v23", "scalar", "Use case: illustration-story. Create one polished editorial satire comic for a serious philosophical article, a wide diptych of two panels side by side. Warm ivory paper, fine dark green ink, muted plum and ochre washes; spare hand-drawn expressive people and architectural absurdity, generous blank space. Same two ordinary adults in both panels, no identifiable real people. Panel 1: a visitor at a small office desk points at a simple EXIT door nearby; administrator smiles with a reassuring open hand. Speech bubble from visitor, verbatim: \"I'd like to leave.\" Speech bubble from administrator, verbatim: \"Of course. Your agency matters.\" Panel 2: a very long winding queue leads back into the same office; the administrator is now behind an enormous stack of forms in front of the EXIT door. Speech bubble from administrator, verbatim: \"First, complete our six-stage departure readiness process.\" The visitor looks quietly incredulous, not distressed. Large clear lettering, all text exact, no additional labels, no logos, no title. Panels must read clearly left to right. Dry humane satire aimed at institutional control disguised as care; no visual cruelty. Flat illustration, not photorealism, no luminous fantasy motifs.")
