("v34", "type", "String")
("v34", "scalar", "Use case: illustration-story. A polished editorial satire comic, two panels side by side on warm ivory paper. Fine dark green pen contours, restrained plum and ochre watercolor, quiet deadpan humor and lots of clear space. Same two fictional ordinary adults both panels. An office of a benevolent-looking foundation, no real organization or individual. Panel 1: a well-dressed foundation officer ceremoniously hands a very small key to an ordinary visitor, beside a locked cabinet visibly containing money. The officer's speech bubble exactly: \"We funded your right to challenge us.\" Panel 2: visitor holds the key but the cabinet has a second, much larger lock. Officer points to that lock, smiling earnestly, with speech bubble exactly: \"Access to the fund requires our approval.\" Visitor's raised eyebrow is the punchline. Make the physical absurdity of a useless key immediately legible. Large beautifully legible lettering, exact quoted text only, no title, no other labels, no logos. Aim satire at the proposed correction framework itself: control retained through support. No villains, no mockery of vulnerability, no luminous fantasy motifs, no photorealism.")
("v33", "value", "v34")
